## 3. Contract essentials (pass verbatim)
- **Port:** `process.env.PORT || 3000`; base `http://localhost:3000`; startup log exactly `listening on http://localhost:${port}`.
- **API `GET /api/message`:** 200 `{"message":"hello world"}` · null → **503** `{"error":"no message in database"}` · throw → **500** `{"error":"..."}` + `console.error` with stack. Unknown path/non-GET → 404 `{"error":"not found"}`. All `application/json`.
- **`src/db.js`:** `export function getMessage()` — **synchronous**, returns `string` | `null` (null also when table missing, i.e. unseeded DB must not throw), throws on unexpected SQLite errors. DB path **must** be `new URL('../data/hello.db', import.meta.url)`. Named export only.
- **`src/seed.js`:** idempotent; `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, body TEXT NOT NULL)`; ensures exactly one row `body='hello world'`; logs what it did; non-zero exit on failure.
- **Static:** `public/` at web root; `/` → `index.html`; `/styles.css`, `/app.js`; types for `.html .css .js .svg .woff2`; reject `..` traversal.
- **DOM hooks:** `<body class="page">` › `<main class="hero">` › `<section class="card" data-state="loading">` containing `<p id="message" class="message">` and `<p id="status" class="status" aria-live="polite">`. Head: `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">`, `<script type="module" src="/app.js"></script>`. **State is only** `data-state="loading"|"ready"|"error"` on `.card` — no other state classes.
- **CSS scope:** `.page, .hero, .card, .message, .status, [data-state=...]` only; must not demand new markup; responsive + `prefers-color-scheme` + `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Run:** `npm run seed && npm start`, then the curl sequence in CONTRACT.md §9.

## 4. npm install
**Not run and not required** — zero dependencies by design. `package.json` validated as loadable JSON with the correct scripts.

## 5. Deviations / cautions
- No `node_modules`, no lockfile: downstream agents must not introduce one.
- `src/` and `public/` are empty directories (git won't track them until files land); the owning agents create their files directly — that is intentional, no stubs to overwrite.
- Watch out: `getMessage()` is **sync**, not a Promise — the backend agent must not `await`-assume a Promise contract (awaiting a string still works, but the 503/500 branching must handle the sync signature and the `null` case explicitly).


